{"title":"Fair","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>If an object, especially a coin or die, is considered \"fair\", it is not skewed and has an equal probability of producing any of its outputs. For example, a fair coin has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> chance of landing heads and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> chance of landing tails. Similarly, a fair six-sided die has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f34b3cf20be89133434c1a52cb3bbc3342a16664.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> chance of showing any positive integer from 1 to 6, inclusive, on its top face.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Fair&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018030312\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.005 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.009 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 16/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 253/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 519/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.402      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.402      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17916:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018030312 and revision id 112944. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}